# HELP lith_prefetch_unread_resident_bytes Bytes HELD IN THE MEMORY TIER that nothing has read. This -- not lith_prefetch_committed_bytes -- is the quantity eviction-before-read is about: committed counts from dispatch and so includes bytes still in flight, which cannot evict anything. Compare against --mem-cache, not --prefetch-budget: the collapse condition is this approaching tier CAPACITY, at which point every arriving chunk must evict an unread one (#313).
