lith_prefetch_unread_resident_bytes 0
# HELP lith_prefetch_used_total Prefetched chunks TOUCHED by a later demand read (same 1 MiB unit as lith_prefetch_issued_total). A CHUNK-TOUCH count, not a byte count: a 64 KiB read marks the whole 1 MiB chunk used, so used/issued OVERSTATES byte follow-through, and overstates it most for the scattered readers where prefetch is least useful. Measured case: 89% by this ratio against at most ~25% of the prefetched bytes actually read. Do not read it as a byte efficiency (#256).
